Package: spatialSVP
Type: Package
Title: Spatially Variable Pathway Activity in Spatial Transcriptomics
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Liubo", family = "Li", role = c("aut",
        "cre"), email = "liliubo@189.cn", comment = c(ORCID =
        "0000-0002-7325-0102"))
Description: Tests whether pathway activity estimates vary spatially
        across tissue sections, bridging the gap between pathway
        activity scoring tools and gene-level spatial variability
        tests. Activity can be computed from gene sets with several
        back ends (mean z-score aggregation, decoupleR mlm/wmean,
        fgsea, GSVA), optionally after regressing out library size and
        top expression principal components, then tested for spatial
        variability with statistics inspired by Moran's I, SPARK-X
        covariance kernels, and SpatialDE Gaussian-process models, the
        latter providing pathway-level length scales. Significance can
        be assessed against an absolute null (shared-permutation
        Westfall-Young maxT correction, respecting the correlation of
        pathway scores from a shared expression matrix) or a relative
        null comparing each pathway with size- and expression-matched
        random gene sets. Block-aware kernels and permutations support
        multi-section or multi-patient designs. Inputs can be plain
        matrices, SpatialExperiment, or Seurat objects.
